    "nome": "Francesco Pesce",
    "ruolo": "Systematic Theology",
    "bio": Theological anthropology of family relationships: the family experience as revealing the original dimension of the “us” of every human being; the articulations between genders and generations as the possibility of a profound understanding of sexuality, love, and fertility in light of the Christian faith; the social dimension of love and family.
Family life and relationships as a theological place: pastoral theology of marriage and the family, with attention to the dimension of accompaniment and training within the family and in an interdisciplinary key
Marriage theology in an ecumenical key, particularly intermarriage and Lutheran theology."
